      {
        "narration": "May 23, 1964. Cumberland, England. Jim Templeton snapped a photo of his young daughter sitting in a quiet meadow.",
        "visual_keywords": "grassy field sunny day"
      },
      {
        "narration": "When the film developed, a figure in a white space suit was standing right behind her. Kodak inspected the original negative\u2014it was completely untouched.",
        "visual_keywords": "vintage photo development"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Jim Templeton stated that the only other people in the area that day were a couple of elderly women sitting in a car at the far end of the marsh.",
        "visual_keywords": "empty scenic meadow"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Photo analysts finally solved it. The 'spaceman' was Jim\u2019s wife walking away\u2014her light blue dress bleached pure white by camera overexposure, and her dark hair mimicking a visor.",
        "visual_keywords": "camera lens focus"
      },
      {
        "narration": "One of history\u2019s most famous alien photos wasn\u2019t an extraterrestrial visitor\u2014just a very overexposed mom.",
        "visual_keywords": "old family photo"
      }
